{# The two controls a page of either plane carries: the language, which the provider ships as structure and
   words and this application draws as a control of the bar, and the theme, which is this application's
   alone (issues #448 and #447). They are in one file because the two skeletons place them in two places.

   The radio button that is checked while nothing is open comes first, and the veil that checks it again
   comes last: one group of radio buttons is what makes a single control open at a time, and the veil over
   the page is what makes a click anywhere else close it. Neither is a script; a page of this plane runs
   none. A skeleton may add a control of its own after the include, the user menu of the account being one:
   the group is named here and the veil is read wherever it sits. #}
<input type="radio" name="layout-control" id="layout-control-none" aria-label="{{ 'controls.close'|trans([], 'beffroi') }}" checked>
{% include '@Beffroi/_locale_switcher.html.twig' %}
{% include '_theme_switcher.html.twig' %}
<label for="layout-control-none" data-control="veil" aria-hidden="true"></label>
